[Term]
id: PROMOT:0032012
name: Debilidad fatigable de la musculatura facial
def: "A type of weakness of the facial musculature (i.e. one or more muscles innervated by the seventh cranial nerve) that occurs after a muscle group is used and lessens if the muscle group has some rest. That is, there is diminution of the strength of the facial musculature with repetitive muscle actions." [] {IAO:0000119="HP:0003473"}
