[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100005
name: Assessment of expiratory and cough peak flows using an expiratory flowmeter
def: "A test assessing the subject’s expiratory peak flow when they expirate and when they cough. It assesses the glottis efficiency to clear out the repiratory tract by using an expiratory flowmeter." []
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure
is_a: PROMOT:0100002 ! Body function related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100007
name: Assessment using Dysphagimeter
def: "An assessment that uses the Dysphagimeter scale to assess dysphagia or swallowing impairements. The Dysphagimeter is a patient-reported questionnaire that measures the ability to swallow foods of different textures and the impact of dysphagia on activities and participation. This questionnaire has three parts. Part A includes 24 items concerning solid foods, Part B includes 3 items on liquids and Part C includes 8 items, namely 6 items on the impact of dysphagia at meal times and 2 items on discomfort related to thick saliva. Each item offers 5 choices of descriptive answers. Parts A and B also include an option 'I cannot answer'. The participant must carefully read the instructions and check the answer that best corresponds to their situation for each item." [] {IAO:0000119="Definition translated from French to English using Reverso."}
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100008
name: Assessment of pinch strengh using B & L gauge
def: "An evaluation procedure that uses a B&L gauge to assess pinch strengh. The test measuring the force of the lateral clamps, between the thumb and the index finger, allows quantifying the maximum voluntary strength of the hand and forearm muscles during a pinching action. This is an indicator of the level of hand function." [] {IAO:0000119="Definition translated from French to English from a Reverso’s suggestion."}
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100009
name: Assessment of the maximum isometric muscle strength using MedUP dynamometer
def: "Assessment of the maximum isometric muscle strength of flexor and extensor muscles using MedUP dynamometer. It assesses the maximum isometric muscle strength in upper and lower limbs." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)"}
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100010
name: Assessment of tongue strengh using Iowa Oral Performance Instrument
def: "Assessment of the strengh of the tongue muscle by using Iowa Oral Performance Instrument." []
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100011
name: Assessment using Berg Balance Scale
def: "An assessment with the Berg scale assesses balance and identifies the level of fall risk. This five-level ordinal scale (0 to 4) contains 14 items and the maximum total score ranges from 0 (maximum reach) to 56 (no reach detected). This generic scale evaluates various dimensions of balance, including the following: maintaining multiple positions, having automatic postural responses when changing posture or voluntary movements of the limbs, and produce effective balance and protection reactions." [] {IAO:0000119="Automatically translated from French."}
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100012
name: 10 Meter Walk Test (10MWT)
def: "Le 10mwt est un test de capacité qui permet d’évaluer la vitesse de marche sur une courte distance pour deux conditions différentes, soit à la vitesse confortable et à la vitesse maximale. Le temps requis pour parcourir 10 mètres à la marche d’abord à la vitesse confortable, puis à la vitesse maximale, est inscrit." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)."}
xref: http://snomed.info/id/431527001
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100013
name: Assessment using Sydney Swallow Questionnaire (SSQ)
def: "Le questionnaire sur la déglutition de Sydney est un questionnaire auto-rapporté qui a pour but d’évaluer la gravité des problèmes de déglutition. Il comporte 17 questions. Le participant répond aux questions 1 à 11 et 13 à 17 en traçant un X sur une ligne (questions de type échelle visuelle analogue) et à la question 12 en cochant la réponse de son choix parmi 6 options. Une version canadienne-française validée a été créée." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)."}
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100014
name: 80 ml water swallowing test
def: "L’objectif de ce test est de boire 80 ml d’eau le plus rapidement possible sans s’étouffer. L’évaluateur déclanche le chronomètre quand les lèvres du participant touchent l’eau et l’arrête quand le participant dit « STOP »." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)."}
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100015
name: Assessment using Fatigue Severity Scale (FSS)
def: "Assessment using Fatigue Severity scale. It follows a 9-item scale which measures the severity of fatigue and its effect on a person's activities and lifestyle in patients with a variety of disorders.  A 9-item questionnaire with questions related to how fatigue interferes with certain activities and rates its severity according to a self-report scale. The items are scored on a 7 point scale with 1 = strongly disagree and 7= strongly agree. The minimum score = 9 and maximum score possible = 63. Higher the score = greater fatigue severity. Another way of scoring: mean of all the scores with minimum score being 1 and maximum score being 7. Lerdal (2011) found that items 1 and 2 in the FSS-9 should not be used in a mean score because the FSS-7 shows better validity and reliability and is likely more sensitive for measuring change in fatigue." [] {IAO:0000119="Source for the definition of the scale: https://www.sralab.org/rehabilitation-measures/fatigue-severity-scale"}
comment: Krupp, L. B., LaRocca, N. G., Muir-Nash, J., & Steinberg, A. D. (1989). The fatigue severity scale. Application to patients with multiple sclerosis and systemic lupus erythematosus. Archives of Neurology, 46(10), 1121–1123. 
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100016
name: Assessment using Hand Jamar dynanometer
def: "Le test mesurant la force de préhension permet de quantifier la force maximale volontaire des muscles de la main et de l’avant-bras, lors d’une action de flexion des doigts. Il s’agit d’un indicateur du niveau de fonction de la main." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)."}
xref: http://snomed.info/id/445993006
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100017
name: Stair Climb Test
def: "Le test de 10 marches évalue la capacité à monter et descendre un bloc de 10 marches pour deux conditions différentes, soit à la vitesse confortable et à la vitesse maximale. Ce test s’adressent aux participants qui ont la capacité d’utiliser les escaliers." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)."}
xref: http://snomed.info/id/252482003
is_a: PROMOT:0100001 ! Phenotypically related procedure

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0110001
name: Actividad
def: "Actividad es la realización de una tarea o acción por parte de una persona. Las limitaciones en la actividad son dificultades que una persona puede tener para realizar una tarea o acción." [] {IAO:0000119="Clasificación Internacional del Funcionamiento, de la Discapacidad y de la Salud"}
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso ICF:1394728112

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0120002
name: Participación
def: "A participation is an involvement in a life situation. Participation restrictions are problems an individual may experience in involvement in life situations" [] {IAO:0000119="International Classification of Functioning, Disability and Health (ICF)"}
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso ICF:1394728112

[Typedef]
id: PROMOT:2000001
name: es utilizado por
def: "A relation between an assistive device and a patient, where the patient uses the device in order to accomplish something, such as a task or an activity (e.g. moving, reading)." []
comment: JP: Translated to spanish using Bing Translator
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: PROMOT:2000002
name: assesses
def: "A relation between an evaluation procedure and the entity assessed by the procedure that could be a patient or a phenotype. The evaluation procedure could be, for instance, a performance test, a patient reported questionnaire or a scale (non restrictive)." []
comment: JP: Translated to spanish using Bing Translator
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: PROMOT:2000003
name: measures
def: "A relation between an evaluation procedure and the entity measured by the procedure, such as a structure, a function, an activity or a participation." []
xref: SCDO:1000194
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: PROMOT:2000004
name: est porteur de la mutation
def: "A relation between an organism and a specific gene mutation that exists in the genome of that organism." []
xref: VO:0001039
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: PROMOT:2000005
name: affecte
def: "A relation between two entity where the first entity affects the state of the second entity." []
xref: BIOLINK:affects
xref: SIO:001158
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: PROMOT:2000006
name: is related to
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: PROMOT:2000007
name: has identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: RO:0000080
name: quality of
def: "a relation between a quality and an independent continuant (the bearer), in which the quality specifically depends on the bearer for its existence" []
comment: This relation is modeled after the BFO relation of the same name which was in BFO2, but is used in a more restricted sense - specifically, we model this relation as functional (inherited from characteristic-of). Note that this relation is now removed from BFO2020.
property_value: IAO:0000112 "this red color is a quality of this apple" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "A quality inheres in its bearer at all times for which the quality exists." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000118 "is quality of" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000118 "quality_of" xsd:string
inverse_of: RO:0000086 ! has quality

[Typedef]
id: RO:0000086
name: has quality
def: "a relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a quality, in which the quality specifically depends on the bearer for its existence" []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "this apple has quality this red color" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "A bearer can have many qualities, and its qualities can exist for different periods of time, but none of its qualities can exist when the bearer does not exist." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000118 "has_quality" xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: RO:0000091
name: has disposition
def: "a relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a disposition, in which the disposition specifically depends on the bearer for its existence" []

[Typedef]
id: RO:0001025
name: located in
def: "a relation between two independent continuants, the target and the location, in which the target is entirely within the location" []
subset: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/valid_for_go_gp2term
property_value: IAO:0000111 "located in" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "my brain is located in my head" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "this rat is located in this cage" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "Location as a relation between instances: The primitive instance-level relation c located_in r at t reflects the fact that each continuant is at any given time associated with exactly one spatial region, namely its exact location. Following we can use this relation to define a further instance-level location relation - not between a continuant and the region which it exactly occupies, but rather between one continuant and another. c is located in c1, in this sense, whenever the spatial region occupied by c is part_of the spatial region occupied by c1.    Note that this relation comprehends both the relation of exact location between one continuant and another which obtains when r and r1 are identical (for example, when a portion of fluid exactly fills a cavity), as well as those sorts of inexact location relations which obtain, for example, between brain and head or between ovum and uterus" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "Most location relations will only hold at certain times, but this is difficult to specify in OWL. See http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/docs/temporal-semantics/" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000118 "located_in" xsd:string
property_value: RO:0001900 RO:0001901
property_value: seeAlso "https://wiki.geneontology.org/Located_in" xsd:anyURI
property_value: terms:source "http://www.obofoundry.org/ro/#OBO_REL:located_in" xsd:string
is_transitive: true

[Typedef]
id: RO:0002200
name: has phenotype
def: "A relationship that holds between a biological entity and a phenotype. Here a phenotype is construed broadly as any kind of quality of an organism part, a collection of these qualities, or a change in quality or qualities (e.g. abnormally increased temperature). The subject of this relationship can be an organism (where the organism has the phenotype, i.e. the qualities inhere in parts of this organism), a genomic entity such as a gene or genotype (if modifications of the gene or the genotype causes the phenotype), or a condition such as a disease (such that if the condition inheres in an organism, then the organism has the phenotype)." []
subset: ro-eco
property_value: IAO:0000114 IAO:0000125
property_value: IAO:0000117 https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165

[Typedef]
id: RO:0002234
name: has output
def: "p has output c iff c is a participant in p, c is present at the end of p, and c is not present in the same state at the beginning of p." []
subset: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/valid_for_go_annotation_extension
subset: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/valid_for_go_ontology
subset: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/valid_for_gocam
subset: ro-eco
property_value: IAO:0000114 IAO:0000125
property_value: IAO:0000117 https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165
property_value: IAO:0000118 "produces" xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso "https://wiki.geneontology.org/Has_output" xsd:anyURI

[Typedef]
id: RO:0002328
name: functionally related to
def: "A grouping relationship for any relationship directly involving a function, or that holds because of a function of one of the related entities." []
property_value: IAO:0000117 https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165
property_value: IAO:0000232 "This is a grouping relation that collects relations used for the purpose of connecting structure and function" xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: RO:0002331
name: involved in
def: "c involved_in p if and only if c enables some process p', and p' is part of p" []
property_value: IAO:0000117 https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165
property_value: IAO:0000118 "actively involved in" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000118 "enables part of" xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso "https://wiki.geneontology.org/Involved_in" xsd:anyURI
is_a: RO:0002328 ! functionally related to

[Typedef]
id: RO:0002351
name: has member
def: "has member is a mereological relation between a collection and an item." []
property_value: IAO:0000119 "SIO" xsd:string
property_value: RO:0001900 RO:0001901

[Typedef]
id: RO:0002614
name: is evidence with support from
def: "A relationship between a piece of evidence and an entity that plays a role in supporting that evidence." []
comment: In the Gene Ontology association model, this corresponds to the With/From field
property_value: IAO:0000112 "An instance of a sequence similarity evidence (ECO:0000044) that uses a homologous sequence UniProtKB:P12345 as support." xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: RO:0004003
name: has material basis in germline mutation in
property_value: seeAlso ORDO:317343
inverse_of: RO:0004013 ! is causal germline mutation in
created_by: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165
creation_date: 2017-11-05T02:45:54Z

[Typedef]
id: RO:0004013
name: is causal germline mutation in
def: "Relates a gene to condition, such that a mutation in this gene is sufficient to produce the condition and that can be passed on to offspring[modified from orphanet]." []
property_value: seeAlso ORDO:317343
created_by: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165
creation_date: 2017-11-05T02:56:40Z

[Typedef]
id: RO:0004029
name: disease has feature
def: "A relationship between a disease and some feature of that disease, where the feature is either a phenotype or an isolated disease." []
created_by: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165
creation_date: 2017-12-26T19:50:53Z

